What do you expect the complexity T(n) of the inorder method of the LinkedBinaryTree to be?

Each node is processed once, and each recursive call does constant work.

Therefore:
T(n) = T(nL) + T(nR) + O(1)

Since nL + nR = n - 1,
T(n) = O(n)

So the expected time complexity is:
O(n)

Linear time.

